# Output
Based on my analysis of the code evidence, here is the guard vocabulary:

**Rule restated:** An acceptance criterion violates if it names a code construct (library, hook, context, interface, import, internal field, mock file) instead of stating what a user perceives (draft content appearing in preview).

**Blacklist** (implementation vocabulary — traceable to code evidence):

| Term | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `contentstackcontext` | React context symbol exported from `src/context/ContentstackContext.ts`; naming it in an AC dictates the implementation mechanism for distributing CMS content. |
| `usecontent` | Custom hook in `src/hooks/useContent.ts`; wraps `useContext(ContentstackContext)` and returns `getContentByKey`. Naming it prescribes the consumption pattern. |
| `createcontext` | React API call in `ContentstackContext.ts` (`createContext<IContentstackContext>({})`); naming it dictates the context-creation mechanism. |
| `usecontext` | React hook imported and called in `useContent.ts`; naming it prescribes the React API used to read context. |
| `usecallback` | React hook imported and used in `useContent.ts` to memoize `getContentByKey`; naming it dictates a React optimization construct. |
| `getcontentbykey` | Internal function returned by `useContent()`; naming it prescribes the specific retrieval API rather than the outcome of content being available. |
| `getvalue` | Utility imported from `utils/getValue` in `useContent.ts`; naming it dictates the internal path-resolution utility. |
| `icontentstackcontext` | TypeScript interface in `ContentstackContext.ts` defining the context shape; naming it prescribes the internal type contract. |
| `icontentstackpage` | TypeScript interface in `src/interface/content/page.ts`; naming it dictates the internal page type rather than the observable page content. |
| `contenttypes` | Constant imported from `constants/contentstack` in `ContentstackContext.ts`; naming it prescribes an internal enum/key type. |
| `modular_blocks` | Internal Contentstack data-structure field name on `IDetailPageStandard` and `IStationFlexiblePage`; naming it dictates the CMS schema field rather than the visible component. |
| `sidebar_modular_blocks_bottom` | Internal Contentstack data-structure field name visible in `content.mock.ts`; naming it prescribes the schema path for sidebar content. |
| `entryembedable` | Type imported from `@contentstack/utils` in `page.ts`; naming it dictates a specific vendor SDK type. |
| `content.mock` | Mock data file referenced in the manifest (`ContentstackAccordion/content.mock.ts`, `ContentstackColorComponent/content.mock.ts`); naming a test double is explicitly forbidden by the rule. |

**Whitelist** (observable surface — what a content author or tester perceives):

| Term | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `live preview` | The observable feature: a content author sees draft content rendered as it will appear. |
| `draft` | Observable state of content being authored but not yet published. |
| `draft content` | Observable: unpublished content the author is editing. |
| `draft entries` | Observable: unpublished CMS entries the author wants to preview. |
| `cms` | The system the content author interacts with; part of the observable surface. |
| `content` | What the user sees on the website; the observable payload. |
| `website` | Where content is displayed to end users; observable destination. |
| `content author` | The user role described in the story; observable persona. |
| `preview` | The observable behavior of seeing content before publishing. |
| `header` | Observable content area a user sees (also a field on `IContentstackContext`, but whitelist wins). |
| `footer` | Observable content area a user sees (also a field on `IContentstackContext`, but whitelist wins). |
| `page` | Observable content area a user navigates and sees. |
| `directories` | Observable directory listings a user browses (also a field on `IContentstackContext`, but whitelist wins). |
| `accordion` | Observable UI component a user interacts with (appears in mock data but is user-facing). |
| `color card` | Observable UI component a user sees (appears in mock data but is user-facing). |
| `protected pages` | Observable limitation noted in story context: certain pages cannot be previewed. |
| `protected content` | Observable limitation noted in story context: certain content cannot be previewed. |
